This repository ports ReStreet, FIFA Street (2012) recompiled, by
SamuelitoDaVila to ARM64 Linux.
ReStreet: https://github.com/samuelit0davila/fifa-street-pc-port
Copyright (c) 2026 SAMUELITODAVILA, MIT License; see its CREDITS.md for its
contributors (among them Emran_Ahm3d).
The patches in patches/ change ReStreet and its patch of the ReXGlue SDK;
the scripts download both from their own repositories at build time.

ReXGlue SDK: https://github.com/rexglue/rexglue-sdk
Copyright (c) 2026, Tom Clay, with portions derived from the Xenia project
(Copyright (c) 2022, Ben Vanik and Xenia project contributors).

The shader math and shared memory texel buffer changes in patches/sdk (0003,
0004) are ported from shiftglue-sdk, Pinyon Shift's fork of the ReXGlue SDK:
https://github.com/arcanite24/shiftglue-sdk, under the same license as the
ReXGlue SDK. Most of patches/sdk, the scripts, the launcher and
tools/steam_art.cpp come from the Saints Reborn ARM64 port
(https://github.com/Ken5998/saints-reborn-arm64) by the same author.

The disc image is read with xiso_extract from Saints Reborn
(https://github.com/whompay/SaintsReborn, Copyright 2026 Whompay, Apache
License 2.0), downloaded at build time at the commit and checksum in
upstream.json; it is not stored here.

The Steam artwork is drawn on the player's machine from the box art, title
screen and icon in the player's checkout of ReStreet, read with stb_image
(public domain, from the SDK's thirdparty folder); none of it is stored here.

The toolchain setup follows pinyon-shift-arm64
(https://github.com/Ken5998/pinyon-shift-arm64) and uses the ARM64 sysroot it
publishes.

